module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.SolvableGroupStructure

import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.RationalRepresentationComoduleDictionary
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.AffineNormalQuotientGeometry

/-! # Extensions of smooth unipotent algebraic groups

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Section 6.45, printed p.135; Proposition 14.3,
Theorem 14.5 and Corollary 14.12, printed pp.280--283
(blueprint: lem-sfb-smooth-unipotent-extension).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SolvableGroupStructure

/-- An extension of smooth unipotent affine algebraic groups is unipotent.
Here unipotence is the recorded faithful geometric matrix condition, and the quotient
condition includes flatness, surjectivity, local finite presentation and the specified
scheme-theoretic kernel. No connectedness or characteristic assumption is needed.

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Section 6.45, printed p.135; Proposition 14.3,
Theorem 14.5 and Corollary 14.12, printed pp.280--283
(blueprint: lem-sfb-smooth-unipotent-extension).

Proof plan, following the seven steps of the DAG node:
1. The faithful closed matrix embeddings of N and Q are injective on all algebra-valued
   points. Apply lem-sfb-geometric-unipotence-unitriangular-embedding to obtain closed
   embeddings of N and Q into unitriangular groups of positive sizes a and b.
2. For any nonzero finite-dimensional rational E-module V, restrict to N. The theorem
   lem-sfb-unitriangular-subgroup-rational-fixed-vector gives a nonzero vector v fixed
   over every commutative k-algebra. By lem-sfb-rational-representation-comodule-dictionary
   its restricted coaction is v mapped to v tensor 1.
3. The quotient in lem-sfb-affine-normal-quotient-geometry and Q represent the same
   fppf sheaf, hence are canonically isomorphic respecting the quotient maps. Thus q is
   faithfully flat on coordinate algebras. Apply
   lem-sfb-central-kernel-cyclic-representation-descent: the cyclic E-subcomodule W
   generated by v is nonzero, finite-dimensional and N-trivial, and descends to Q.
   This descent needs neither centrality nor connectedness.
4. Apply lem-sfb-unitriangular-subgroup-rational-fixed-vector to W as a Q-module.
   It gives a nonzero Q-fixed w. Since the E-action is pulled back along q, w is also
   E-fixed over every test algebra; its image in V remains nonzero.
5. Induct on dim V to obtain a full rational flag with trivial successive quotients.
   For dimension zero use the empty flag. Otherwise the fixed line kw is trivial;
   the coaction descends to V/kw by the dictionary, since the projected coaction
   vanishes on kw. Counitality and coassociativity descend. Lift the inductive flag
   along V to V/kw and prepend kw. Scalar extension preserves it by linear splitting.
6. Apply lem-sfb-normal-subgroup-representation-kernel to the trivial normal subgroup
   of E, cut out by the augmentation ideal. Obtain a positive-dimensional matrix
   representation r with trivial scheme-theoretic kernel. Equality of images of x,y
   on any test algebra implies y inverse times x is in that kernel, so x = y. Apply
   lem-sfb-geometric-unipotence-faithful-closed-immersion to make r a closed immersion.
7. Choose a basis adapted to the flag of this faithful representation. Over every
   test algebra the matrices preserve the flag and act trivially on its quotients,
   so are upper unitriangular. In dimension d their difference from the identity
   has d-th power zero. This holds over every algebraically closed extension.
   Conjugating the original closed immersion by the basis change preserves both
   closed immersion and nilpotence, giving exactly IsUnipotent E.
-/
theorem isUnipotent_of_isFppfQuotient
    {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    (N E Q : Grp (Over (Spec (.of k))))
    [Smooth N.X.hom] [IsAffine N.X.left]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType N.X.hom] [QuasiCompact N.X.hom]
    [Smooth E.X.hom] [IsAffine E.X.left]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType E.X.hom] [QuasiCompact E.X.hom]
    [Smooth Q.X.hom] [IsAffine Q.X.left]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType Q.X.hom] [QuasiCompact Q.X.hom]
    (i : N ⟶ E) (q : E ⟶ Q)
    [IsClosedSubgroupScheme i.hom.hom] [IsNormalSubgroupScheme i.hom.hom]
    (hq : IsFppfQuotient i.hom.hom q)
    (hN : IsUnipotent N) (hQ : IsUnipotent Q) : IsUnipotent E := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.SolvableGroupStructure
